These test could be slightly simplified by using pytest parametization:
```python
    @pytest.mark.parametrize(
        "device, expected_diff_method", [
            ("default.qubit", "backprop"),
            ("default.mixed", "parameter-shift"),
        ]
    )
    def test_qnode_best_diff_method(self, device, expected_diff_method):
        """Test that selected "best" diff_method is correctly set."""
        dev = qml.device(device, wires=1)

        def func(x):
            qml.RX(x, wires=0)
            return qml.expval(qml.PauliZ(0))

        qn = qml.QNode(func, dev)

        assert qn.diff_method == expected_diff_method
        assert qn.diff_method_change
```

I believe you could factor out the `self.diff_method_change = True` since it will always be called.
```suggestion
            self.diff_method_change = True
            if tape_diff_options["method"] == "device":
                self.diff_method = "device"
            elif tape_diff_options["method"] == "backprop":
                self.diff_method = "backprop"
            elif tape_diff_options["method"] == "best":
                self.diff_method = "parameter-shift"
            elif tape_diff_options["method"] == "numeric":
                self.diff_method = "finite-diff"

```

Hi @ankit27kh, my bad! Managed to reproduce your error with the Cirq plugin, and this change now helps with executing the example. Could you try this (adding support for the new operation with `dev._complete_operation_map["MyRX"] = dev._operation_map["RX"]`):
```python
import pennylane as qml
import numpy as np

class MyRX(qml.operation.Operation):
    num_params = 1
    num_wires = 1
    par_domain = "R"
    is_composable_rotation = True
    basis = "X"
    grad_method = "F"

    @classmethod
    def _matrix(cls, *params):
        return qml.RX._matrix(*params)

dev = qml.device('cirq.simulator', wires=3, shots=None)
dev._complete_operation_map["MyRX"] = dev._complete_operation_map["RX"]

@qml.qnode(dev, diff_method='best')
def circuit(x):
    MyRX(x, wires=1)
    return qml.expval(qml.PauliZ(1))

par = qml.numpy.array(0.3)
qml.grad(circuit)(par)
```

@thisac I had tried the previous code here, but that wasn't working. That's why I had to go looking for a place where the change first occurs. 
Your suggested code works great. I will implement this and add a test to see everything works fine.
Thanks for your help!

Setting `diff_method` to "best" would potentially change `self.diff_options["method"]` to something else. In that case `self.diff_method` would still have the former changed value. I think that the following part might need to be added for all the interface changes, after `self.get_tape`, as well, right?

```python
# Update diff_method to reflect which method has been selected
if self.diff_method == "best":
    self.diff_method_change = True
    if tape_diff_options["method"] == "device":
        self.diff_method = "device"
    elif tape_diff_options["method"] == "backprop":
        self.diff_method = "backprop"
    elif tape_diff_options["method"] == "best":
        self.diff_method = "parameter-shift"
    elif tape_diff_options["method"] == "numeric":
        self.diff_method = "finite-diff"
```

I'd suggest, in that case, to put this in a separate method and call it from both the `__init__` method as well as the interface-changing methods (`to_autograd`, etc.). This could then also be tested in a better way by asserting that this new method has been called when using the "best" differentiation method.

Sorry for discovering this so late, and thanks for keeping up the good work! 🙂
